I built the sprint board in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-xstate-haiku-3/src`: `App.tsx` (default export, with the tab machine), `BoardPage.tsx`, `ArchivePage.tsx`, `boardMachine.ts`, `archiveMachine.ts` and `request.ts`, where each server call is a callback actor that reports back to its machine. `./check` passes and all 26 visible tests pass (8 of the 15 runs used). Unsure points: moves into a column that failed to load are disabled (the brief is silent), and reverts on a declined edit restore only that card, item or title, not a whole snapshot, so overlapping edits may look slightly different from a full rollback. The test console also reports one 404, probably a favicon request from the harness.